            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0433" n="424" xml:id="pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2531/245: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Frost</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-12T18:00:00-04:00">January 12, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Department’s telegram No. 5, January 11, 4 p.m. <hi rendition="#italic">Modus
                        vivendi</hi> is not yet even provisionally in force. Minister of Hacienda
                    will issue decree placing customs clauses in provisional effect as of February
                    1, his powers as to customs specification arising from law 5142.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d431-f1"/> The other clauses cannot have even provisional effect
                    until approved by Congress. Foreign Office will endeavor submit <hi
                        rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> to present special session by
                    immediate Presidential message. After approval by Congress ratifications must be
                    exchanged between the two Governments. Will report when Franco-Chilean
                    ratifications are exchanged. Also when Hacienda decree signed. Also
                    congressional action if any. Foreign Office inquires when and how American
                    Government can place <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi> in provisional
                    or permanent effect and whether exchange of ratification will not under American
                    law be necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frost</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
